921:
A subdivider or developer shall apply for preliminary plat approval by submitting to the city clerk the following:
(a) Name, address and telephone number of the person to whom any notices of hearings by the planning commission shall be sent;
(b) Eight copies of the preliminary plat;
(c) A copy of the soil erosion and sedimentation plan as drawn by a registered surveyor or engineer;
(d) A copy of the soil erosion and sedimentation permit (land disturbance permit) as issued by the certifying authority;
(e) Other related documents as may be appropriate, including, but not limited to, environmental impact permit or stormwater control permit; and
(f) A nonrefundable application fee as established by the city council. This fee shall be required for each phase of any proposed subdivision or land division. Preliminary review shall not begin until established fees have been paid.

928:
After the preliminary plat of a proposed subdivision or land division has been approved by the planning commission, the subdivider or developer may, within one year from such approval, apply for final plat approval by submitting to the city clerk the following:
(a) A request for final plat approval with the name and address of the person to whom any notices of hearings by the planning commission shall be sent;
(b) Nine copies of the final plat with the following certifications: ownership, dedication, surveyors or engineers, water and sewer (described elsewhere in this ordinance [appendix]);
(c) Required technical documents, including, but not limited to, paving certificates, compaction test and related data; and
(d) A nonrefundable application fee as established by the city council. This fee shall be required for each phase of any proposed subdivision or land division.
